ge>78</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8036256</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oxman</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Haynes</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>No magic bullets. A systematic review of 102 trials of interventions to improve professional practice.</article-title><source>CMAJ</source><year>1995</year><volume>153</volume><fpage>1423</fpage><lpage>1431</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7585368</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>